  "answer": "The goal was not met: four of the five scenes have a confirmed hard case and the fifth does not. In two of the four, VaVAM failed with no sideways error at all. Clip 19f339ba fails at recorded speed (S24) and clip 096988dd fails at 1.2x (S8), both by drifting left into a car in the next lane. Clip 0ce6f2a3 fails at 1.4x by running onto a median at a fork (S17). Only clip 09a95ffa needed a sideways error: it fails at +0.1 m and 1.4x but not at 0 m and 1.4x (S14 vs S13). Each of these four rests on a handful of repeats, so their failure ranges reach down only to about the low 0.5s\u20130.6. At S17 and S14 every failure is also flagged as a possible artifact, because the ego ended over 3.5 m from the recording. Triage blames the policy's own steering, not the rendering. The planned corners (\u00b10.3\u20130.5 m, mostly at 1.2\u20131.4x) were never run, and negative (rightward) errors were tried only twice. So this shows which combinations break VaVAM in these scenes, not the worst ones in the grid.",
